{
  "version": 1,
  "_readme": [
    "§8.4 — THE INDIRECTION LAYER. This file is why the game ships playable with assets/sheets/ empty.",
    "Every entry names a `placeholder` function in src/render/placeholder.js, which is drawn whenever",
    "the PNG is missing, 404s, or fails to parse. sprites.js logs once and keeps playing; it never throws.",
    "",
    "To swap in real art: export from Shadow Studio's Sprite Forge (chroma mode, flat magenta #FF00FF —",
    "never green, see landmine 19), drop the pair into assets/sheets/, and fill in `png` and `meta` below.",
    "No code changes. That is the phase 6 gate.",
    "",
    "pivot   pixels from the frame's top-left. AUTHORITATIVE when present, and it OVERRIDES Studio's own",
    "        pivot. Never apply both this and Studio's offset_x/offset_y — that puts the sprite exactly",
    "        double the pivot off (landmine 4). sprites.js#pivotOf states the rule once.",
    "scale   metres per pixel. Keeps the sim in metres and the art in pixels, so re-exporting at a",
    "        different resolution is a one-number fix.",
    "smooth  false for pixel art, true for smooth vector art (landmine 18).",
    "",
    "§8.1 settled that the PENGUIN IS DRAWN IN CODE and that is not a stopgap. These penguin entries",
    "exist so a hand-drawn frame folder COULD be dropped in later, not because one is expected."
  ],

